  "note": "Election of the whole Londonderry Corporation (six councillors and two aldermen for each of the five wards), poll Friday 15 January 1926. The Labour Party, with Nationalist support, contested all five wards; the Journal gives the new Corporation as 16 Labour and 24 Unionist (Derry Journal, 18 January 1926). The Unionist aldermen for East, North and Waterside were returned unopposed and the South aldermanships were contested. The spoiled papers figure is for the ward's poll; the aldermanships were polled the same day."
